{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792779798,"nonce":"cy4hIDLVU4NtcAa8/RKqJ1f2Ja4=","title":"TypeScript: enums and literal types","message":"Module-level numeric, string, const and ambient const enums. Members are evaluated as constant enum expressions (literals, earlier members, other enums' members, top-level constants, Infinity/NaN, unary and binary operators with ToInt32 for bitwise ones, string concatenation and templates). Declarations report TypeScript's errors: member without initializer after a string or computed member, computed string members, computed const enum members, non-finite const enum values, references to later members or later enums, duplicate members, enum names shared with types.\n\nAn enum value is its native f64 or static string; enum identity travels as a checker view, and member types (E.A, E.A | E.B) are views over a member subset. Assignability follows TypeScript: other enums and non-member literals are rejected, plain numbers are accepted by numeric enums, plain strings are not accepted by string enums. Equality comparisons that cannot overlap are rejected using enum members, the members a binding may hold (narrowed by assignment, by === and !== and by while-loop exit), and the literal types of number and string const bindings. Module-level let bindings keep their narrowing across calls at top level as TypeScript does; facts do not cross function boundaries.\n\nExplicit gaps (Unsupported): reverse mapping, enum objects as values, computed members, mixed numeric and string enums, values of ambient non-const enums, declaration merging, exported enums and exported signatures using enums, local enums, and enums in arrays, record or class fields, unions with other types, function types and generic rules. A function that may read a regular enum before its declaration runs checks a flag and traps as the undefined enum object would.\n\nAlso in this cluster: properties of primitives, arrays and unions (x.length, x.toString()) report Unsupported instead of the false Type error \"receiver has no fields\", and reads or writes of ambient `declare var` bindings report Unsupported instead of a false \"used before being assigned\".\n\nParent: 9c8744d1566d3fe158923a8120ef1afd21e259998da54d65bf14df43853fa3b5.","files":null}]}